THOUGHT: Good, GDEF is the right constant for global definitions. Now let me modify the lookup_fully_qualified function to handle the __getattr__ case:

```bash
sed -i '/if key not in names:/,/return None/{
s/if key not in names:/    if key not in names:
        # Check if this module has a __getattr__ that could provide this symbol
        if "__getattr__" in names:
            # Create a placeholder for a symbol that would be provided by __getattr__
            getattr_node = names["__getattr__"]
            if isinstance(getattr_node.node, (FuncDef, Var)):
                from mypy.types import CallableType, AnyType, TypeOfAny
                node_type = getattr_node.node.type
                if isinstance(node_type, CallableType):
                    typ = node_type.ret_type
                else:
                    typ = AnyType(TypeOfAny.from_error)
                v = Var(key, type=typ)
                v._fullname = name
                v.from_module_getattr = True
                return SymbolTableNode(GDEF, v)
        if raise_on_missing:
            assert key in names, f"Cannot find component {key!r} for {name!r}"
        return None
}' ./mypy/lookup.py
